# Settings of the production installation, read by docker-compose.prod.yml. Copy to .env on the server once, replace
# every CHANGE_ME, keep it there: a release replaces docker-compose.prod.yml and the Caddyfile, never .env.
# A value containing $ goes into single quotes ('...'), otherwise compose would read it as a variable.
# The app refuses to start while a secret is still CHANGE_ME (README.md "Configuration").

# The domain Caddy serves and fetches the certificate for, without https://
APP_DOMAIN=CHANGE_ME

# The admin login - the password at least 12 characters
APP_USERNAME=CHANGE_ME
APP_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
# openssl rand -base64 48 - changing it logs the admin out (tenant API keys are not affected)
JWT_GENERATOR_SIGNATURE_SECRET=CHANGE_ME
# openssl rand -base64 32 - encrypts the stored AI provider keys: back it up, losing or changing it means entering them
# again
APP_SECRET_KEY=CHANGE_ME
# openssl rand -base64 48 - only counts when ./pgdata is created; afterwards change it with ALTER ROLE first
DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME

# Optional - the look of the installation (login page, the admin's dashboard, every tenant without its own look, which
# the admin sets per tenant in the frontend). The logo: a PNG, JPEG or WebP of at most 512 KB, copied into the volume
# "files" once (podman cp logo.png alpdesk-ai:/home/app/files/branding-logo.png). An invalid value stops the start.
#APP_BRANDING_NAME=Alpdesk AI
#APP_BRANDING_PRIMARY_COLOR=#49732a
# Without APP_BRANDING_LOGO the Alpdesk AI logo is shown; empty (APP_BRANDING_LOGO=) shows none.
#APP_BRANDING_LOGO=/home/app/files/branding-logo.png

# Optional - the daily report by e-mail (README.md "Daily report"): every morning at 06:00 to these addresses (comma
# separated), also when everything is fine - a missing one means the app or sending mail is down. Without a mail
# server or recipients nothing is sent. APP_MAIL_SECURITY: STARTTLS (port 587), SSL (port 465) or NONE; APP_MAIL_FROM
# defaults to APP_MAIL_USERNAME. A recipient that is no e-mail address, or a mail server without a sender address
# (neither APP_MAIL_FROM nor an address as APP_MAIL_USERNAME), stops the start - the log names the setting.
#APP_MONITORING_MAIL_TO=ops@example.com
#APP_MAIL_HOST=smtp.example.com
#APP_MAIL_PORT=587
#APP_MAIL_SECURITY=STARTTLS
#APP_MAIL_USERNAME=report@example.com
#APP_MAIL_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
#APP_MAIL_FROM=report@example.com
# Another time: a cron expression (seconds minutes hours day month weekday) in the time zone Europe/Berlin.
#APP_MONITORING_DAILY_REPORT_CRON=0 0 6 * * *

# Optional - own model servers (Ollama, OpenAI-compatible; the admin enters them in the model catalog). They are reached
# over HTTPS only; plain HTTP only to the hosts listed here, comma separated (a server in the same pod or the internal
# network, e.g. ollama,10.0.0.5). A listed host is reachable on any port - also as the address of connected software
# (MCP), which every tenant admin enters: never list localhost or the app's own container.
#APP_AI_PLAIN_HTTP_HOSTS=
# A server with a certificate of the company's own authority: copy the authority's certificate (PEM, *.crt) into the
# volume's certificates/ (or mount a folder there) and set 1 (README.md "Own model servers") - the certificate check
# stays on.
#USE_SYSTEM_CA_CERTS=1

# Code execution (Python and shell in the chat) needs nothing here: every tenant that wants it gets a sandbox of its
# own, started from docker-compose.tenant-sandbox.yml with its own file in sandboxes/ (README "Code execution").

# Optional - behind a reverse proxy under a sub-path (e.g. nginx at https://intranet.example.com/alpdesk-ai/): the path,
# without a trailing slash. Everything is then served below it (README.md "Behind a reverse proxy under a
# sub-path", with the nginx configuration).
#MICRONAUT_SERVER_CONTEXT_PATH=/alpdesk-ai

# Optional - sign-in through a WAM proxy in front of the app (README.md "Sign-in through a WAM proxy"):
# tenant users sign in with the user name the proxy sends in APP_WAM_USER_HEADER and have no password; the admin keeps
# APP_USERNAME / APP_PASSWORD. Only with a proxy that removes these headers from every request from outside - and the
# app reachable through it only: the app trusts them completely.
#APP_WAM_ENABLED=true
#APP_WAM_USER_HEADER=X-Remote-User
#APP_WAM_NAME_HEADER=X-Remote-Name
